      "text": [
        "920 - وَ كَانَ رَسُولُ اَللَّهِ صَلَّى اَللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهِ أَتَمَّ اَلنَّاسِ صَلاَةً وَ أَوْجَزَهُمْ كَانَ إِذَا دَخَلَ فِي صَلاَةٍ قَالَ «اَللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ «بِسْمِ اَللّٰهِ اَلرَّحْمٰنِ اَلرَّحِيمِ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.920 - \"The Messenger of Allah (sw) was the most complete in performing prayer and the most concise.\nWhen he began his prayer, he would say: 'Allāhu Akbar (God is the Greatest)' and then recite, 'Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm (In the name of Allah (swt), the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful).'\""
        ]
      }
